angle":{"y":456.82686805725098,"x":689.73957824707031,"width":280.671875,"height":57.600000381469727}},{"text":"Negative rules of belief will tell you when you should not have a certain belief.","targetRectangle":{"y":142.515380859375,"x":644.85090637207031,"width":371.625,"height":96}},{"text":"Truth → Belief","targetRectangle":{"y":431.22686767578125,"x":313.1644287109375,"width":171.9384765625,"height":32}},{"text":"If P is true, you should believe P.","targetRectangle":{"y":456.82686805725098,"x":303.0352783203125,"width":196.9873046875,"height":57.600000381469727}},{"text":"If you think about it, our initial question really breaks down into two sub-questions. ","targetRectangle":{"y":-98.196121215820312,"x":228.08546447753906,"width":738.5625,"height":62}},{"text":"What should I believe?","targetRectangle":{"y":-194.90231323242188,"x":456.97138977050781,"width":253.03955078125,"height":32}},{"text":"If you are in such-and-such circumstances, you should not believe P.","targetRectangle":{"y":806.3031005859375,"x":680.23733520507812,"width":284.6484375,"height":81}},{"text":"When should I form a new belief?","targetRectangle":{"y":35.85882568359375,"x":289.49124145507812,"width":249.4140625,"height":60.799999237060547}},{"text":"It might at first seem extremely easy to formulate the rules of belief. The following would seem to be plausible candidates, respectively, for positive and negative rules of belief.","targetRectangle":{"y":286.67501831054688,"x":250.34141540527344,"width":743.578125,"height":93}},{"text":"When should I discard one of my beliefs?","targetRectangle":{"y":35.85882568359375,"x":671.37953186035156,"width":256.01806640625,"height":60.799999237060547}},{"text":"The problem with these rules of belief is not that they are incorrect; the problem is that in many cases they won’t be of much practical use, since in many cases we don’t know for sure whether the claim in question is true or false. (If we did, there would be no serious question about whe